# Hual02 route (item59, re-authored by item67): player input from the vent spawn to Carrington's
# cell and the exit plateau, objectives driven only by the game's own chains.
#
# Player input (no set_goal/take_control): crouch-crawl through the ceiling vent
# (spawn 104,1840,-4536 -> gallery), two aimed shots break the two grates
# (BreakableMover5 at 104,1192 yaw 270; BreakAbleMover2 at -496,-688 yaw 259.5,
# measured legs 9-12), crawl the duct and drop into the office floor -4856,
# walk the underfloor to the service lift lobby, ride the lift (item67: the game's own
# LiftButton0.PlayerTrigger -> LiftManager states -> LiftCage key move; the player is carried
# by the decoded mover-base attachment), then the surface corridor to the depot.
#
# Labelled teleports, each for a measured movement gap (see the report):
# - "depot"          t=292 (-8880,722): Porte19 is TriggerControl behind the magnetic-card
#                    chain and stays locked in this sim: the only card pickup
#                    (Hual02MagneticCardPick4 at -3474,1550) sits in the petitesalle whose
#                    walkable envelope is sealed from the corridor (measured probe: the walker
#                    is stopped at y=1698 outside and y=1595 inside, x -3461..-3420; the access
#                    runs through the meeting-room chain whose promotion is blocked upstream,
#                    item59's DV21 float and CWndSFXTrigger stall). The route uses the reader
#                    anyway (t=285.5: MyPCPostRender TargetActor=MagneticPassTrigger1,
#                    bCanTrigger=true, Grab runs and PlayerTrigger plays the no-card sound);
#                    Porte19 stays KeyNum=0 (asserted). The landing inside CineTrigger6 also
#                    starts the game's own Carrington scene ('Carring_ShaftEnter').
#                    The corridor west of Porte19 is itself blocked at (-6198,842) in this sim
#                    (measured probe, local/re/item67/out/west.txt), so the teleport also
#                    crosses that gap.
# - "prison entry"   t=298 (-10368,2800): the prison compound perimeter is sealed
#                    in this sim (Porte151 Locked opens only from Carrington's
#                    escort moveseq); the landing touches DetectionVolume14 whose
#                    'didact6' event completes goal 2 through XIIIGoalTrigger1.
# - "prison grille escape" t=304 (-10176,2900): the DV14 landing sits inside the
#                    simplified collision of StaticMeshActor1024 'grille_prison';
#                    measured leg31: the player is pinned until moved.
# - "stair head"     t=352 (-14896,656,438): the exit stairwell pins the walker at
#                    (-14078,1314,35) (measured legs 20-23); the corridor beyond is
#                    sealed by the Locked Porte151, so the exit plateau is entered here.
#
# Weapon grant (labelled diagnostic): the player would carry the Beretta from
# Hual01b (the campaign loadout; Hual01a's route test documents no grant because
# the fresh-login inventory already has it). Starting on Hual02 directly hands the
# Fists only, so the route re-grants xiii.Beretta to make the two grate shots real.
#
# Objectives completed by the game's chains on this route (measured legs 31-37 and the
# fixture runs): goals 4/5/6 complete (the Carrington scene via CineTrigger6 and the
# anti-goal completions), goal 3 promoted by the same scene. The promotion chain for
# goals 1 and 2 is blocked in this sim: DetectionVolume21 ('demarre_bureau', which
# promotes goal 1 through XIIIGoalTrigger3) floats 78 UU above the real duct floor
# (z=-4320, cylinder half-height 40, measured), and the eavesdrop scene's
# 'Blam' -> 'objectif92' promotion of goal 2 stalls at the unimplemented CWndSFXTrigger
# scene action. The DV14 -> 'didact6' -> XIIIGoalTrigger1 completion of goal 2 only
# validates a promoted goal (measured: leg37 with the diagnostic cue vs the fixture).
# (TouchTrigger8 z=63 gallery -> Cine7 'soldat_plan' raid -> 'soldat_assome' ->
# CineTrigger8 CineGoto -> Carrington moveseqs open Porte151 -> 'fin') is blocked:
# TouchTrigger8's gallery and Porte151 are both unreachable on foot in this sim, so
# goal 0 and the travel request stay unmet; the test asserts that measured blocker.
